<title>UK: Gulf maintenance cuts OPEC crude output in May - IEA.</title>
<headline>Gulf maintenance cuts OPEC crude output in May - IEA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC crude oil output in May fell by 280,000 barrels per day (bpd) from April to 26.87 million bpd, the International Energy Agency (IEA) said on Friday.</p>
<p>Maintenance activites at two offshore fields in the United Arab Emirates (UAE) and in the Neutral Zone shared by Saudi Arabia and Kuwait were responsible for the fall, the Paris-based agency said in its monthly Oil Market Report.</p>
</text>
